# Project Cleanup Audit Report

As requested, I have performed a complete static analysis of the Next.js + Supabase application using `knip`, dependency checks, and a full schema dump scan. I have verified imports, exports, API usages, and package dependencies across the entire codebase.

---

## 🔴 SAFE TO DELETE (100% Confidence)
These items have been strictly verified to have **zero** usages across the entire codebase. Deleting these will have **no impact** on application behavior.

### 1. Unused Source Files & Components
- **`src/app/(admin)/admin/students/components/DeleteStudentButton.tsx`**
  - **Reason:** Never imported or rendered in any layout or page.
- **`src/features/notifications/actions/notifications.ts`**
  - **Reason:** Contains `getUnreadNotificationsCount`, `markNotificationAsRead`, etc., which are completely unused (notifications likely fetch directly via Supabase client or another mechanism).
  
### 2. Unused / Dead API Routes
- **`src/app/api/deploy/validate/route.ts`**
- **`src/app/api/github/validate/route.ts`**
  - **Reason:** No `fetch()` calls or backend references point to these endpoints. These appear to be abandoned experimental MVPs.

### 3. Orphaned Scratch/Migration Scripts (Root Directory)
- `analyze_schema.js`, `dump_schema_info.js`, `audit_report.md`
- `apply_*.js`, `fix_*.js`, `test_*.mjs`, `check_*.js`
- `scripts/database/*.js`, `scratch/*`
  - **Reason:** These are throwaway Node scripts used to test queries, apply migrations, and audit schemas. They are not part of the Next.js production build and clutter the repository.

### 4. Unused Dependencies (package.json)
- **`dotenv`**
  - **Reason:** Next.js automatically supports `.env` natively. The package is only used by the scratch scripts listed above.
- **`pg`**
  - **Reason:** Only used by the root node migration scripts. Next.js app uses `@supabase/supabase-js`.
- **Dev Dependencies:** `@types/dompurify`, `postgres`
  - **Reason:** Never imported anywhere in the `src/` directory.

